From 68625aebe3e9a3f32894c0abaac3bafcfccb986b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Torres <46858378+fabiantorrestech@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:36:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Home: custom page sizes with draggable dividers
 (inkOS-Patcher)

Adds "Arrange pages" to the home apps / pages sheet (tap the "x/y apps"
title in Edit Favorites). It lists every home slot in order with one
divider per page break:
- Drag a divider, or tap its arrows, to move apps between pages.
  Dividers stop at their neighbours and at the top and bottom of the
  list; two dividers together make an empty page.
- X removes a divider, "+ Add page" adds an empty last page, "Even
  split" restores the stock layout.
- Save stores one size per page (e.g. "3,0,5") and the new page count.

Home and the Edit Favorites dashed lines follow the saved sizes while
they still match "Number of home apps" and "Number of pages"; changing
either falls back to the stock even split. Logic lives in
ui/HomePageLayout.kt and ui/PageLayoutEditor.kt; upstream files get
small hooks only.

